<!--ID=FCB40C2B-1F9F-4C26-B1A1-CF8E67BE07D1;Version=1|{"Files":{}}-->
<!--ID=5B95B1CC-2C7B-494F-B746-CF22A0E779B7;Version=1|{"Locales":{"en-US":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]},"en-GB":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]}}}-->
<speak xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2001/10/synthesis"
       xmlns:mstts="http://www.w3.org/2001/mstts"
       xmlns:emo="http://www.w3.org/2009/10/emotionml"
       version="1.0"
       xml:lang="en-GB">
  <voice name="en-GB-OllieMultilingualNeural">
    <prosody rate="-10.25%" pitch="-2.25%">
      Jericho was shut up tight because of the people of Israel.<break time="1000ms"/>
      No one went out.<break time="500ms"/>
      No one came in.<break time="1000ms"/>
      The gates were barred, the walls thick and high.<break time="1800ms"/>

      It was a city held together by fear.<break time="500ms"/>
      The people inside had heard what God had done for Israel.<break time="500ms"/>
      They had heard about the parting of the waters.<break time="500ms"/>
      They had heard about the long march through the wilderness.<break time="1000ms"/>
      And so they locked themselves inside their walls and waited.<break time="1800ms"/>

      From the outside, Jericho looked impossible.<break time="500ms"/>
      The stones were ancient and well-fitted.<break time="500ms"/>
      The fortifications had been standing for generations.<break time="500ms"/>
      No army could simply walk up and push them over.<break time="1800ms"/>

      But God was not troubled by the walls.<break time="1000ms"/>
      What seemed impossible to the eye was already settled in the heart of God.<break time="1800ms"/>

      And so God spoke to Joshua.<break time="500ms"/>
      Not with panic.<break time="500ms"/>
      Not with a complicated strategy of war.<break time="500ms"/>
      But with calm certainty.<break time="1000ms"/>
      He had a plan.<break time="1800ms"/>

      Sometimes the walls in our own lives feel just as high and just as old.<break time="500ms"/>
      But God sees what we cannot see from the ground.<break time="1000ms"/>
      He speaks into the silence behind the walls.<break time="1800ms"/>
      And His voice changes everything.<break time="3800ms"/>
    </prosody>
  </voice>
</speak>
